Q: fitToView() and getBoundingBox() return same bounds for all objects in linked model uploaded from .zip A: <p>Note that the <code>viewer.utilities.getBoundingBox</code> method only accepts a single boolean argument (<code>ignoreSelection</code>). That is why it's returning the same bounds. If you want to calculate the bounds of a specific object, you can do that with the following helper code:</p>
<pre><code>getBoundingBox(dbId, model) {
    const tree = model.getInstanceTree();
    const frags = model.getFragmentList();
    let bounds = new THREE.Box3();
    tree.enumNodeFragments(dbId, (fragId) =&gt; {
        let box = new THREE.Box3();
        frags.getWorldBounds(fragId, box);
        bounds.union(box);
    }, true);
    return bounds;
}
</code></pre>

Q: KendoUI display wrong Turkey currency when value over 100K A: <p>Keep in mind that the ordering of when the JavaScript executes matters. If you're trying to set the culture before the JavaScript file is being referenced, then it will default back to whatever your default culture is.</p>
<p>Here is a minimal example of the numbers being formatted properly:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$(() =&gt; {
  // set the culture (after culture script is referenced)
  kendo.culture('tr-TR');

  // define the view model
  const model = kendo.observable({
    lessThan100k: 12232,
    greaterThan100k: 124544
  });

  // bind the model to the DOM
  const container = $('.container');
  kendo.bind(container, model);
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="container"&gt;
    &lt;p data-bind="text: lessThan100k" data-format="n2"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p data-bind="text: greaterThan100k" data-format="n2"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.4.1.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://kendo.cdn.telerik.com/2025.4.1217/js/kendo.all.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://kendo.cdn.telerik.com/2025.4.1217/js/cultures/kendo.culture.tr-TR.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
